# size-ratchet exclusion list — binary, generated, and append-only log content
# only. Hand-written source is never excluded; oversized source is frozen in
# size-ratchet-baseline.tsv.
# Format: pattern<TAB>reason (shell glob against the full repo-relative path; * crosses /).
# A `!` pattern carves its matches back into the measured set and beats every
# row above or below it — the only way to govern hand-written source that
# lives inside a tree the render rows exclude.

.agents/*	kendex's render of skills/, whose SOURCE is governed, so governing the mirror doubles every finding and freezes the render
!.agents/hooks/*	adopted hook scripts: this tree IS the source, so the row above must not cover it
!.agents/skills/app-deploy/*	in-place skill (kendex-local.toml): this tree IS the source, so the row above must not cover it
!.agents/skills/kendex-issues/*	in-place skill (kendex-local.toml): this tree IS the source, so the row above must not cover it
.claude/skills/*	rendered skill links into .agents/skills
.claude/agents/*	kendex-rendered agent copies, source in agents/
.claude/hooks/*	kendex-rendered hook copies, source in hooks/
.codex/agents/*	kendex-rendered agent copies, source in agents/
.codex/hooks/*	kendex-rendered hook copies, source in hooks/
.pi/agents/*	kendex-rendered agent copies, source in agents/
.pi/kendex/hooks/*	kendex-rendered hook copies, source in hooks/

*.lock	lockfile (Cargo.lock, flake.lock) — generated by the package manager, size is not a design signal
*package-lock.json	npm lockfile — generated by npm
pi-extensions/pi-claude-bridge/bundle/*.js	esbuild output — built from src/ by `npm run build`, reproduced by CI
pi-extensions/*/assets/*	extension screenshots and demo recordings (png/gif/mp4) — binary media
docs/assets/*	documentation screenshots and renders — binary/exported media
skills/iced-rs/examples/*.png	vendored upstream iced example images — binary
skills/iced-rs/examples/*.jpg	vendored upstream iced example textures — binary
skills/iced-rs/examples/*.gif	vendored upstream iced example recordings — binary
skills/iced-rs/examples/*.ttf	vendored upstream iced example fonts — binary
ui/src/bindings.ts	generated by tauri-specta — regenerated from Rust types, never hand-edited
ui/src/components/ui/*	shadcn-generated UI primitives — vendored generated code
docs/img/*	README screenshots and the tour gif — binary media
kendex-local.toml	this repo's own install state — the CLI writes one table per declared item, so it grows with the install and has no seam a person can split
crates/app/gen/schemas/*.json	tauri-build output — capability schemas regenerated on every build of crates/app, never hand-edited
crates/app/icons/*	tauri bundle icons (png/ico/icns) — binary media, not reviewable text
